v, k)` (jira)","Plan: 'every definition site yields exactly ONE (kind,name) entry. This is correctness, not tidiness.'","Baseline shape uses bare `<name>`; nothing in the plan qualifies a config/flag name by its section"],"finding":"The baseline key `<kind>::<name>` is not section-qualified, but `_SECTIONS` contains the same key name in multiple sections — `allow_insecure` is an `_as_bool` key in BOTH `reconciler` and `jira`. Two distinct definition sites therefore collapse into one `feature_flag::allow_insecure` entry, so removing one section's key (while the other persists) shows no delta and a future same-named boolean key in a third section is silently admitted — contradicting the plan's 'every definition site yields exactly ONE (kind,name) entry' pillar.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3e1d6ae0cc99b42c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — partition paragraph and Baseline shape (`{\"<kind>::<name>\": 1}`); AC1","norm_id":"n22a8eaa53733cd4f","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Delete `jira.allow_insecure` while `reconciler.allow_insecure` remains: census still emits `feature_flag::allow_insecure`, so the removal is invisible and AC10's removal semantics are unreliable for colliding names","A new `foo.allow_insecure` boolean key added later matches an existing baseline entry and passes the ratchet unjustified"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Define the `name` for config_key/feature_flag as `<section>.<key>` and state that AC1 disjointness plus the 'one site = one entry' pillar are tested against the section-qualified name.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes