undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile AC2/AC3 with the 'never hardcoded' Testing note: state whether the counts are asserted as literals (76/27) at introduction or via a structural partition invariant.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["COH"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.131,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Testing: 'Census counts are derived LIVE from the tree, never hardcoded'","AC2: 'Verified by a test asserting its live count is 76.'","AC3: 'Verified by a test asserting its live count is 27.'"],"finding":"The Testing section states census counts are 'derived LIVE from the tree, never hardcoded,' but AC2 and AC3 verify by 'asserting its live count is 76' and '...is 27' — a specific numeric oracle. If the count is derived live, asserting equality to a literal 76/27 IS a hardcoded expectation, contradicting the 'never hardcoded' discipline.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faed236e3877eac54","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section vs AC2/AC3","norm_id":"n9de7e93016b1554b","priority":0.469,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor cannot tell whether to write `assert count == 76` (hardcoded oracle) or a structural invariant (e.g. config_key + feature_flag == total _SECTIONS entries, boolean partition)."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Frame AC2/AC3 as partition invariants: assert config_key and feature_flag counts SUM to the total _SECTIONS entries and that feature_flag is exactly the boolean-coerced subset — rather than asserting bare literals 76/27.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State that boolean-coerced `_SECTIONS` entries are identified by AST-parsing `_config_sections.py` (matching `_as_bool` in each key's coercer lambda), not by reading the runtime `_SECTIONS` dict whose values are opaque closures.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.332,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: `config_key` detection = '`_config_sections._SECTIONS`, excluding boolean-coerced entries'; `feature_flag` = 'the boolean-coerced `_SECTIONS` entries'","src/rebar/_config_sections.py:32 `\"enforce_plan_material_pins\": lambda v, k: _as_bool(v, k)` — values are closures; the runtime dict cannot reveal which coercer a lambda calls","The partition is the stated correctness pillar ('every definition site yields exactly ONE (kind,name) entry'), and AC2/AC3 assert exact counts (76/27) derived from it"],"finding":"The config partition (config_key vs feature_flag) claims to read the runtime `_config_sections._SECTIONS` dict, but boolean-coercion is not decidable from that runtime object: every value is an opaque `lambda v, k: _as_bool(v, k)` / `_as_int(...)` closure, so 'the boolean-coerced entries' can only be identified by AST-inspecting the source of `_config_sections.py` for the coercer each lambda calls.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8f8049c875e3686d","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — detection table (`config_key` / `feature_flag` rows) and the partition paragraph","norm_id":"ndad9cd7395fad676","priority":0.268,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A test derives the live boolean set from the runtime dict and finds every lambda indistinguishable, so config_key/feature_flag cannot be split as specified"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Change the `config_key`/`feature_flag` detection column to 'AST scan of `src/rebar/_config_sections.py`: a `_SECTIONS` key whose coercer lambda calls `_as_bool` is a `feature_flag`, all others `config_key`', mirroring how `gen_env_registry.py` AST-classifies rather than importing runtime objects.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the ESLint prior-art framing: note that eslint-suppressions.json records a scalar `count` per (file,rule) bucket (tradeable within a bucket), and state that this plan DELIBERATELY departs from that by using a presence-keyed value-always-1 (kind,name) entry so no kind can be traded — rather than citing ESLint as the shape being ported.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'The baseline is keyed per (kind, name) — never a scalar sum — per the ESLint eslint-suppressions.json shape (12c), so one kind cannot be traded against another.'","Retrieved eslint.org blog 'Introducing bulk suppressions' (2025-04): 'This file contains the number of violations for each rule and file ... \"no-undef\": { \"count\": 1 }' — a scalar count per (file,rule) bucket.","Retrieved GitHub eslint/eslint#21226: 'The suppressions file records a count per (file, rule), not per specific violation' — confirming within-bucket count is exactly what ESLint tracks (and can be swapped).","The plan's own shape uses a constant value 1 per (kind,name), i.e. presence-keyed, which is a departure from ESLint's per-bucket count, not the same shape."],"finding":"The plan cites ESLint's eslint-suppressions.json as the shape precedent for a per-(kind,name), value-always-1 baseline that is 'never a scalar sum', but the actual ESLint format records a scalar `count` per (file,rule) bucket (e.g. {\"no-undef\": {\"count\": 1}}) — the opposite property. The prior art is mischaracterized: the plan is departing from ESLint's shape, not porting it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6b42828a6c08e08e","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context section ('per the ESLint eslint-suppressions.json shape (12c)') and 'Baseline and modes' ({\"<kind>::<name>\": 1})","norm_id":"n81b84a1d33d43023","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or future maintainer checks the cited ESLint precedent and finds it does the opposite, undermining confidence in the stated rationale for the keying design.","The '12c' internal reference is trusted to justify no-scalar-sum keying when the external source it leans on actu